@startuml raditrack_activity_audit_log_and_undo_upload
!theme plain
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155

title RADiTrack — Activity Diagram: Reviewing the Audit Log and Undoing an Upload

|Administrator|
start
:Open Configuration → **Audit log**;

if (View?) then (Exam changes)
  repeat
    :Filter by accession, action, source,\nuser, date range or real / test data;
    :Read the changes, newest first (50 per page):\ntime, user, accession, what happened,\nsource / file, before → after values;
  repeat while (Look at another exam or filter?) is (yes)
  ->no;
  stop
else (Uploads)
endif

|RADiTrack|
:List every upload with file, user, time,\nrows, changes and result;
:Offer **Undo upload** where the quick checks pass\n(successful "Add or update" upload,\nwithin the amendment window,\nsame data loaded, not undone yet);

|Administrator|
if (Undo an upload?) then (no)
  :Review the uploads\n(**View changes** shows what each did);
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Press **Undo upload**;

|RADiTrack|
:Check the upload in full: was any of its exams\nchanged or deleted afterwards (a later audit entry,\nor values no longer the ones it wrote)?;
if (Can it be undone?) then (no)
  :Show the reason and the exams\nchanged since; nothing is changed;
  |Administrator|
  stop
else (yes)
endif
:Show what will happen\n(exams to remove, exams to restore);

|Administrator|
if (Confirm?) then (no)
  stop
else (yes)
endif

|RADiTrack|
:Lock imports and the upload's exam rows;
:Check again (nothing may have\nchanged in between);
:In one transaction:\nremove the exams the upload added;\nput back the values it changed or amended\n(including removing sign-offs it added);
:Record each exam in the audit trail\n("Removed by undo" / "Restored by undo");
:Mark the upload as **Undone**\n(by whom and when);
:Refresh dashboard and other open tabs;

|Administrator|
:See "Upload undone: N removed, N restored";
stop

@enduml
